---
import LegalPage from '../../components/LegalPage.astro';

const supportEmail = 'hello@m8tcha.com';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Refund Policy"
  description="How M8tcha handles subscription cancellations, refunds, and billing issues."
>
  <p>
    This Refund Policy applies to M8tcha Premium subscriptions and other paid features. It should be
    read with our{' '}<a href="/legal/terms">Terms of Service</a>{' '}and{' '}
    <a href="/legal/pricing">Pricing</a>{' '}page. Nothing here limits a refund or cancellation right that
    cannot legally be waived.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Canceling a Subscription</h2>
  <p>
    Canceling stops future renewals; it does not normally create a partial-period refund. For Stripe
    purchases, use the manage-subscription link in the app or Stripe Customer Portal. For Apple or
    Google purchases, cancel in your Apple Account or Google Play subscription settings. You normally
    keep Premium access until the end of the period already paid for.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    We may issue a full or partial refund when required by law or when a payment was duplicated,
    unauthorized, materially incorrect, or a paid feature was unavailable and we cannot reasonably
    restore it. Refunds are returned to the original payment method where possible. Approved Stripe
    refunds can take several business days to appear, depending on the card issuer.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not promise refunds for unused time after cancellation, dissatisfaction with interactions
    with another user, or failure to use a paid feature, except where applicable law requires one.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Where to Request Help</h2>
  <p>
    For a Stripe charge, email <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a> with the account
    email, charge date, amount, and reason for the request. Do not send full card numbers or security
    codes. We may ask for information sufficient to verify the account and transaction.
  </p>
  <p>
    Apple and Google control refunds for purchases made through their stores. Request those refunds
    directly from Apple at <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>
    or through Google Play's refund process. We cannot issue a store refund for a transaction we did
    not process.
  </p>

  <h2>4. EU/UK Consumer Rights</h2>
  <p>
    Consumers in the EU, EEA, or UK may have a statutory cooling-off or withdrawal right. If you ask
    us to begin supplying a digital service immediately, you may lose that right once performance has
    begun, to the extent permitted by law. Any mandatory local consumer rights remain unaffected.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
